119-**Labels.** Every claim has exactly one label.
120-
121-- **PROVED**: the full proof is in this note. One model wrote it, and no second model or human has re-derived
122-  it yet (RESEARCH_PLAN §4, rule 3).
123-- **CONJECTURE**: not proved. The text names the evidence that would settle it. "Scratch evidence" means a
124-  throwaway script run once in the session scratchpad (geometry plus a small retrograde solver, Appendix A):
125-  not kpsolve, not saved in the project, not independently checked.
126-- **KNOWN**: from the literature, with a citation.
127-- **COMPUTED-1** and **CHECKED-2** (revised after K19, 2026-10-27): labels for a finite computation, never for a
128-  theorem. COMPUTED-1: one implementation produced the numbers. CHECKED-2: two independently written
129-  implementations agree on the exact numbers (for example the scratch run and a second program, or two solvers).
130-  Neither label is a proof, and neither replaces PROVED for a statement over all contexts.
131-
132-kpsolve results (§6) are data, not proofs: a claim that only a kpsolve run supports keeps the label
133-CONJECTURE (for a statement over all contexts) or COMPUTED-1 (for the finite computation itself), with
134-"kpsolve agrees" (revised after review: R1 item 6; after K19, 2026-10-27: CHECKED-2 needs a second, independently
135-written implementation, and a second run of the same code or of a build derived from it does not count).
