397-- **(a)** Induction on the total height.
398-  - At a reachable non-terminal Y′, each option of the CGT sum is one of two kinds.
399-    - A move in some y′_j to a non-terminal position. The induction hypothesis applies to it.
400-    - A move to the integer σB in coordinate j, giving σB + Σ_{i≠j} (y′_i)^B. By dominance this is in 𝓛 if
401-      σ = ⊕ and in 𝓡 if σ = ⊖. That is exactly the status of the D-option "σ wins now".
402-  - No other options exist, because no integer summand is present yet.
403-  - So the options correspond one to one with the D-options of Y′, with the same "won by Left with Right to
404-    move" status. The same holds on the Right side.
405-  - A player with no option loses in both.
406-- **(b)** Take σ = ⊕; the case σ = ⊖ is symmetric.
407-  - Let Y′ be reachable from Y without passing a terminal, and let y′_j → ⊕ be the option, made by either
408-    player. Since the option exists, + ∈ τ(y′_j) (Definition 1.10, corrected: an option counts whoever makes
409-    it). By pairwise safety no other coordinate has − ∈ τ(y′_i); by monotonicity of τ no other coordinate can
410-    ever reach ⊖, so no option of the sum Σ_{i≠j}(y′_i)^B is −B. This is the step that failed for the earlier
411-    τ, which was blind to a ⊕ entered by Right (revised after review: R1 item 1, R2 item 1).
412-  - The frontier position is B + Σ_{i≠j}(y′_i)^B, and the positive integer B has canonical form {B−1 | } (a
413-    Left-only stack of B moves, [WW] ch. 2), so Right has no move in it.
414-  - Left's strategy: on every turn, play in a positive integer summand (the B created by the event, or a +B
415-    created later), and never in a component.
416-  - Right's moves are all moves in the components, and there are at most M_R(Y) of them: the moves in one
417-    coordinate form a sequence of moves in that coordinate, so the total is at most Σ_{i≠j} M_R(y′_i) ≤ M_R(Y)
418-    (M is monotone, and for a sum M is the sum over the coordinates). A Right move into a terminal can only
