2382-  - the decisive event has T = 0 with White to move and T = 1 with Black to move;
2383-  - Proposition 2.10(a) gives (L2), because Black cannot promote in one move from a non-terminal context; for Black to move this is Theorem 2.7(b), the window form, with Q = the position itself, and (L3) is the one-turn check that Black is not stalemated: its Z-pawn g7 has the moves g6 and g5 in every context; if Y carries an e.p. right, (L2) counts it, and it cannot promote at once (revised after K7, 2026-10-22);
